{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AYs8KKQmmP2ANhEyDZNZ7X","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Task-specificity characterization of equalizer effect\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"对 6 个 benchmark 计算 1.3B 下各 attention ratio 的 cross-architecture std， 建立 convergence strength（Spearman ρ）与 retrieval demand 的连续关系。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"lambada_rho\": -1.0,\n7\t      \"lambada_std_reduction_pct\": 79,\n8\t      \"arc_easy_rho\": -0.7,\n9\t      \"arc_challenge_rho\": -0.3,\n10\t      \"hellaswag_rho\": -0.1,\n11\t      \"winogrande_rho\": 0.05,\n12\t      \"mmlu_rho\": 0.1,\n13\t      \"benchmarks_with_rho_below_neg05\": 2\n14\t    },\n15\t    \"tables\": [\n16\t      {\n17\t        \"name\": \"Table 1: Cross-architecture convergence by benchmark\",\n18\t        \"columns\": [\n19\t          \"Benchmark\",\n20\t          \"Retrieval Demand (BIG-bench)\",\n21\t          \"ρ (std vs attn ratio)\",\n22\t          \"p-value (permutation)\",\n23\t          \"Std at ratio=0\",\n24\t          \"Std at ratio=24\"\n25\t        ],\n26\t        \"rows\": [\n27\t          [\n28\t            \"LAMBADA\",\n29\t            \"High\",\n30\t            \"-1.00\",\n31\t            \"0.0083\",\n32\t            \"0.024\",\n33\t            \"0.005\"\n34\t          ],\n35\t          [\n36\t            \"ARC-Easy\",\n37\t            \"Medium-High\",\n38\t            \"-0.70\",\n39\t            \"0.117\",\n40\t            \"0.031\",\n41\t            \"0.018\"\n42\t          ],\n43\t          [\n44\t            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n45\t            \"Medium\",\n46\t            \"-0.30\",\n47\t            \"0.347\",\n48\t            \"0.022\",\n49\t            \"0.019\"\n50\t          ],\n51\t          [\n52\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n53\t            \"Low\",\n54\t            \"-0.10\",\n55\t            \"0.782\",\n56\t            \"0.018\",\n57\t            \"0.017\"\n58\t          ],\n59\t          [\n60\t            \"WinoGrande\",\n61\t            \"Low-Medium\",\n62\t            \"0.05\",\n63\t            \"0.912\",\n64\t            \"0.015\",\n65\t            \"0.016\"\n66\t          ],\n67\t          [\n68\t            \"MMLU\",\n69\t            \"Low\",\n70\t            \"0.10\",\n71\t            \"0.782\",\n72\t            \"0.028\",\n73\t            \"0.027\"\n74\t          ]\n75\t        ]\n76\t      }\n77\t    ],\n78\t    \"figures\": [],\n79\t    \"analysis\": \"Continuous retrieval-demand spectrum 成立。避免了 binary retrieval/reasoning 分类的 post-hoc cherry-picking 风险。BIG-bench taxonomy 提供外部锚定。LAMBADA + ARC-Easy 两个锚点形成梯度，其余 benchmark 填充低端。Reviewer Concern B 通过 dose-response framing 化解。\\n\\n\\nLAMBADA 是纯 last-word retrieval 任务，attention 的 key-value lookup 机制天然对齐 这类需求，因此跨架构方差压缩最彻底（ρ=-1.0）。ARC-Easy 含大量事实检索型题目， attention 部分有效（ρ=-0.7）。HellaSwag/WinoGrande/MMLU 以推理、常识、世界知识为主， attention 的收敛作用被 recurrence core 的架构差异主导，ρ 趋近零。这形成了以 retrieval demand 为横轴的 dose-response 曲线，两个显著锚点（LAMBADA + ARC-Easy）足以建立 continuous spectrum 的可信度。\\n\"\n80\t  },\n81\t  {\n82\t    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\",\n83\t    \"description\": \"对 1.3B 模型（GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 × 5 attention ratios）和 10×340M 模型重新运行 lm-eval --log_samples，收集 HellaSwag、ARC-Easy、ARC-Challenge 的 per-example 数据。 分析 per-example 层面是否存在 convergence 或 task-specific divergence。\\n\",\n84\t    \"results\": {\n85\t      \"hellaswag_per_example_convergence\": false,\n86\t      \"hellaswag_per_example_pattern\": \"systematic architecture-specific, not random noise\",\n87\t      \"arc_easy_per_example_convergence\": true,\n88\t      \"arc_easy_rho_after_per_example\": -0.85,\n89\t      \"arc_easy_jaccard_pairwise\": 0.12,\n90\t      \"arc_challenge_per_example_convergence\": false,\n91\t      \"arc_challenge_per_example_pattern\": \"weak, architecture-independent noise\",\n92\t      \"models_evaluated\": 23,\n93\t      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 18\n94\t    },\n95\t    \"tables\": [\n96\t      {\n97\t        \"name\": \"Table 2: Per-example convergence metrics by benchmark\",\n98\t        \"columns\": [\n99\t          \"Benchmark\",\n100\t          \"N samples\",\n101\t          \"Aggregate ρ\",\n102\t          \"Per-example ρ (filtered)\",\n103\t          \"Jaccard (pairwise mean)\",\n104\t          \"Pattern type\"\n105\t        ],\n106\t        \"rows\": [\n107\t          [\n108\t            \"LAMBADA\",\n109\t            \"5153\",\n110\t            \"-1.00\",\n111\t            \"-1.00\",\n112\t            \"0.06\",\n113\t            \"Architecture-specific convergence\"\n114\t          ],\n115\t          [\n116\t            \"ARC-Easy\",\n117\t            \"2376\",\n118\t            \"-0.70\",\n119\t            \"-0.85\",\n120\t            \"0.12\",\n121\t            \"Retrieval-subset convergence\"\n122\t          ],\n123\t          [\n124\t            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n125\t            \"1172\",\n126\t            \"-0.30\",\n127\t            \"-0.25\",\n128\t            \"0.31\",\n129\t            \"No systematic pattern\"\n130\t          ],\n131\t          [\n132\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n133\t            \"10042\",\n134\t            \"-0.10\",\n135\t            \"-0.08\",\n136\t            \"0.22\",\n137\t            \"Systematic but non-converging\"\n138\t          ]\n139\t        ]\n140\t      }\n141\t    ],\n142\t    \"figures\": [],\n143\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-002 的 best 结果是双重确认：(1) HellaSwag/ARC-C 在 per-example 层面确认非收敛， 升级 task-specificity 从\\\"aggregate insignificant\\\"到\\\"per-example confirmed non-converging\\\"； (2) ARC-Easy 在去噪后 ρ 加强至 -0.85，成为第二个强锚点。Continuous spectrum 从 单点（LAMBADA）变为双锚点梯度，极大加强 Claim 1。\\n\\n\\nHellaSwag 在 aggregate 层面无收敛（ρ=-0.1），per-example 分析确认这不是 power 问题而是 真阴性——attention 在不同架构上改变不同 sample 的正确率，但这些变化是 systematic architecture-specific（每个架构有自己稳定的 helped/hurt subset），而非 random noise。 这说明 attention 在推理任务上\\\"做了事\\\"但没有跨架构趋同。ARC-Easy 在 per-example 层面 发现 attention 确实压缩了跨架构差异：对 retrieval-heavy 子题（事实召回型），三个架构的 正确率 variance 下降；对 reasoning-heavy 子题则无变化。这将 aggregate ρ 从 -0.70 加强至 -0.85（通过去除 reasoning 子题噪声）。ARC-Easy 成为 continuous spectrum 的 第二个强锚点。ARC-Challenge 因推理占比高，per-example 无系统模式。\\n\"\n144\t  },\n145\t  {\n146\t    \"name\": \"Helped/hurt sample characterization\",\n147\t    \"description\": \"对 LAMBADA 上各架构的 helped/hurt samples 计算 token frequency、context length、 last-sentence perplexity、domain 分布。测试 feature 是否区分 helped/hurt，且跨架构 feature profile 是否不同。\\n\",\n148\t    \"results\": {\n149\t      \"n_features_significant_p001\": 3,\n150\t      \"best_feature\": \"target_token_frequency\",\n151\t      \"best_feature_p\": 2.5e-05,\n152\t      \"second_feature\": \"context_length\",\n153\t      \"second_feature_p\": 0.00031,\n154\t      \"third_feature\": \"last_sentence_perplexity\",\n155\t      \"third_feature_p\": 0.00087,\n156\t      \"gdn_profile\": \"helped on rare tokens + long contexts\",\n157\t      \"retnet_profile\": \"helped on high-perplexity last sentences\",\n158\t      \"hgrn2_profile\": \"helped broadly but strongest on medium-frequency tokens\",\n159\t      \"cross_arch_profile_difference_p\": 0.0003,\n160\t      \"effect_size_cohens_d_best\": 0.72\n161\t    },\n162\t    \"tables\": [\n163\t      {\n164\t        \"name\": \"Table 3: Feature importance for helped/hurt classification by architecture\",\n165\t        \"columns\": [\n166\t          \"Feature\",\n167\t          \"GDN (AUC)\",\n168\t          \"RetNet (AUC)\",\n169\t          \"HGRN2 (AUC)\",\n170\t          \"Overall p-value\",\n171\t          \"Cross-arch difference p\"\n172\t        ],\n173\t        \"rows\": [\n174\t          [\n175\t            \"Target token freq (log rank)\",\n176\t            \"0.71\",\n177\t            \"0.58\",\n178\t            \"0.64\",\n179\t            \"2.5e-05\",\n180\t            \"0.0012\"\n181\t          ],\n182\t          [\n183\t            \"Context length (tokens)\",\n184\t            \"0.67\",\n185\t            \"0.55\",\n186\t            \"0.57\",\n187\t            \"3.1e-04\",\n188\t            \"0.0089\"\n189\t          ],\n190\t          [\n191\t            \"Last-sentence perplexity\",\n192\t            \"0.56\",\n193\t            \"0.69\",\n194\t            \"0.61\",\n195\t            \"8.7e-04\",\n196\t            \"0.0003\"\n197\t          ],\n198\t          [\n199\t            \"Domain (topic entropy)\",\n200\t            \"0.54\",\n201\t            \"0.53\",\n202\t            \"0.55\",\n203\t            \"0.042\",\n204\t            \"0.31\"\n205\t          ]\n206\t        ]\n207\t      }\n208\t    ],\n209\t    \"figures\": [],\n210\t    \"analysis\": \"3 个 feature 在 p<0.001 水平显著区分 helped/hurt，且跨架构 profile 统计显著不同。 这为 Claim 3（architecture-specific mechanism）提供了 feature-level 解释：不是抽象的 \\\"不同 sample\\\"，而是\\\"不同语言学特征的 sample\\\"。Feature profile 差异直接映射到各架构 recurrence core 的已知机制特性（delta rule → rare token recall; exponential decay → local disambiguation; hierarchical gating → multi-scale memory）。\\n\\n\\nGatedDeltaNet 的 delta rule 机制擅长 associative recall，attention 补充的是对 rare token 的 precise retrieval（delta rule 对 rare token 的 update 不够精确）， 因此 GDN helped samples 集中在 rare token + long context（需要远距离检索）。RetNet 的 exponential decay 使其对 last sentence 内的局部信息较强，attention 补充的是 high-perplexity last sentence 中的 disambiguation（decay 无法区分多个候选），因此 RetNet helped samples 集中在 high-perplexity last sentence。HGRN2 的 hierarchical gating 提供多尺度记忆但对 token frequency 有 sweet spot，attention 拓宽了这个 sweet spot。三种架构的 feature profile 统计显著不同（p<0.001），这直接解释了为什么 Jaccard overlap 低——它们被 attention 帮助的 sample 具有不同的语言学特征。\\n\"\n211\t  },\n212\t  {\n213\t    \"name\": \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\",\n214\t    \"description\": \"从 h3-1 配置的三个架构提取 attention weight，分析 attention pattern 与 per-example helped/hurt identity 的相关性，以及跨架构 attention pattern 的相似度。\\n\",\n215\t    \"results\": {\n216\t      \"attention_per_example_correlation_gdn\": 0.52,\n217\t      \"attention_per_example_correlation_retnet\": 0.61,\n218\t      \"attention_per_example_correlation_hgrn2\": 0.48,\n219\t      \"attention_per_example_correlation_mean\": 0.54,\n220\t      \"cross_arch_attention_similarity\": 0.23,\n221\t      \"gdn_attention_focus\": \"distributed over long-range context tokens\",\n222\t      \"retnet_attention_focus\": \"concentrated on last-sentence tokens\",\n223\t      \"hgrn2_attention_focus\": \"hierarchical — split between local and mid-range\",\n224\t      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 3.5\n225\t    },\n226\t    \"tables\": [\n227\t      {\n228\t        \"name\": \"Table 4: Attention pattern analysis\",\n229\t        \"columns\": [\n230\t          \"Architecture\",\n231\t          \"Attention focus\",\n232\t          \"Corr with helped/hurt\",\n233\t          \"p-value\",\n234\t          \"Mean entropy\"\n235\t        ],\n236\t        \"rows\": [\n237\t          [\n238\t            \"GDN\",\n239\t            \"Long-range distributed\",\n240\t            \"0.52\",\n241\t            \"1.2e-04\",\n242\t            \"3.41\"\n243\t          ],\n244\t          [\n245\t            \"RetNet\",\n246\t            \"Last-sentence concentrated\",\n247\t            \"0.61\",\n248\t            \"8.7e-06\",\n249\t            \"2.18\"\n250\t          ],\n251\t          [\n252\t            \"HGRN2\",\n253\t            \"Hierarchical split\",\n254\t            \"0.48\",\n255\t            \"4.3e-04\",\n256\t            \"2.89\"\n257\t          ]\n258\t        ]\n259\t      },\n260\t      {\n261\t        \"name\": \"Table 4b: Cross-architecture attention similarity (cosine)\",\n262\t        \"columns\": [\n263\t          \"Pair\",\n264\t          \"Mean cosine sim\",\n265\t          \"Significance vs random baseline\"\n266\t        ],\n267\t        \"rows\": [\n268\t          [\n269\t            \"GDN-RetNet\",\n270\t            \"0.19\",\n271\t            \"p<0.001 (below random)\"\n272\t          ],\n273\t          [\n274\t            \"GDN-HGRN2\",\n275\t            \"0.27\",\n276\t            \"p=0.003 (below random)\"\n277\t          ],\n278\t          [\n279\t            \"RetNet-HGRN2\",\n280\t            \"0.24\",\n281\t            \"p=0.001 (below random)\"\n282\t          ]\n283\t        ]\n284\t      }\n285\t    ],\n286\t    \"figures\": [],\n287\t    \"analysis\": \"Mean correlation 0.54（range 0.48–0.61）超过 pass_fail 阈值 0.4，提供了 mechanistic evidence 的第二根支柱。与 exp-003 的 feature 分析合在一起，形成完整因果链： recurrence core 特性 → attention 学到补偿性 pattern → 补偿作用在不同语言学特征 的 sample 上生效 → 各架构 aggregate 性能趋同但 per-example 效果不重叠。 这回应 Reviewer Concern C（\\\"no causal mechanism\\\"），从 correlation 升级到 directed mechanistic narrative。\\n\\n\\nAttention layer 在不同 recurrence backbone 上学到了不同的 attention pattern，因为 它在补偿各架构 recurrence core 的不同弱点。GDN 的 delta rule 已经做了一定的 associative memory，attention 学会关注 long-range context（补充 delta rule 的 远距离衰减）。RetNet 的 exponential decay 快速遗忘远距离信息，attention 集中在 last-sentence 内做 disambiguation（因为 RetNet 对近距离信息已经较强）。HGRN2 的 hierarchical gating 在多个尺度上保留信息但每个尺度都不够精确，attention 学会 hierarchical 分配。这些不同的 attention pattern 与 helped/hurt sample 的对应关系 ≥0.4（最高 RetNet 0.61），因为 attention 的\\\"关注什么\\\"直接决定了\\\"帮助哪些 sample\\\"。 跨架构 attention similarity 仅 0.23，远低于随机基线 0.5，这是 mechanistic evidence 的核心：同样的 attention 架构在不同 recurrence backbone 上学到了完全不同的行为。\\n\"\n288\t  },\n289\t  {\n290\t    \"name\": \"Architecture expansion check\",\n291\t    \"description\": \"搜索 Wang et al. model zoo 及其他来源，找到额外的 hybrid 架构（Mamba hybrid 等）， 在 LAMBADA 上评估收敛模式是否复现。\\n\",\n292\t    \"results\": {\n293\t      \"additional_architectures_found\": 1,\n294\t      \"architecture_name\": \"Mamba2-Attn hybrid (from community reproduction)\",\n295\t      \"architecture_type\": \"selective state space + attention\",\n296\t      \"lambada_convergence_confirmed\": true,\n297\t      \"mamba2_rho\": -0.9,\n298\t      \"mamba2_std_reduction_pct\": 71,\n299\t      \"mamba2_jaccard_with_others\": 0.05,\n300\t      \"total_architectures_tested\": 4,\n301\t      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 5\n302\t    },\n303\t    \"tables\": [\n304\t      {\n305\t        \"name\": \"Table 5: Architecture expansion — convergence on LAMBADA\",\n306\t        \"columns\": [\n307\t          \"Architecture\",\n308\t          \"Recurrence type\",\n309\t          \"ρ (std vs attn ratio)\",\n310\t          \"Std reduction %\",\n311\t          \"Jaccard with GDN\",\n312\t          \"Jaccard with RetNet\",\n313\t          \"Jaccard with HGRN2\"\n314\t        ],\n315\t        \"rows\": [\n316\t          [\n317\t            \"GDN\",\n318\t            \"Gated delta rule\",\n319\t            \"-1.00\",\n320\t            \"79%\",\n321\t            \"—\",\n322\t            \"0.06\",\n323\t            \"0.04\"\n324\t          ],\n325\t          [\n326\t            \"RetNet\",\n327\t            \"Linear attn + exp decay\",\n328\t            \"-1.00\",\n329\t            \"79%\",\n330\t            \"0.06\",\n331\t            \"—\",\n332\t            \"0.08\"\n333\t          ],\n334\t          [\n335\t            \"HGRN2\",\n336\t            \"Hierarchical gating\",\n337\t            \"-1.00\",\n338\t            \"79%\",\n339\t            \"0.04\",\n340\t            \"0.08\",\n341\t            \"—\"\n342\t          ],\n343\t          [\n344\t            \"Mamba2-Attn\",\n345\t            \"Selective state space\",\n346\t            \"-0.90\",\n347\t            \"71%\",\n348\t            \"0.05\",\n349\t            \"0.04\",\n350\t            \"0.07\"\n351\t          ]\n352\t        ]\n353\t      }\n354\t    ],\n355\t    \"figures\": [],\n356\t    \"analysis\": \"Mamba2-Attn 的加入将 architectures_tested 从 3 提升到 4，覆盖了四种不同的 recurrence mechanism。收敛模式复现（ρ=-0.90, std reduction 71%），且 Jaccard 保持低水平， 说明 equalizer effect 不是三个特定架构的巧合，而是 attention + any recurrence 的 通用现象。这是 generalization evidence 的最佳结果，直接提升论文的 impact 和 reviewer 的信任度。\\n\\n\\nMamba2 的 selective state space mechanism 与 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 的 linear recurrence 不同（selection mechanism vs gating/delta rule/exponential decay），但 attention 的补偿效应仍然成立：Mamba2 的 state selection 对某类 retrieval pattern 较弱， attention 补充后 aggregate 性能趋同。ρ=-0.90（略弱于 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 的 -1.0） 可能因为 Mamba2 hybrid 的 attention 集成方式略有不同（interleaved vs stacked）， 但趋势一致。Jaccard 0.05 表明 Mamba2 的 helped/hurt subset 与其他三个架构同样 不重叠，进一步支持 architecture-specific mechanism。n=4 架构使得 Reviewer Concern D （\\\"n=3 too few\\\"）大幅缓解。\\n\"\n357\t  },\n358\t  {\n359\t    \"name\": \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\",\n360\t    \"description\": \"深入分析 340M 在 attn=8 时的非单调 rebound。与 1.3B 同 attention ratio 做 per-example 对比，识别 diverge 的 sample 并 characterize rebound 机制。\\n\",\n361\t    \"results\": {\n362\t      \"rebound_mechanism\": \"capacity bottleneck\",\n363\t      \"rebound_explanation\": \"340M 在 attn ratio=8 时，attention 参数占总参数比例过高（~30%）， 压缩了 recurrence core 的有效容量。Recurrence core 性能下降的 sample 与 attention 新帮助的 sample 不完全重叠，导致 aggregate std 回升。\\n\",\n364\t      \"rebound_samples_n\": 412,\n365\t      \"rebound_samples_overlap_with_1_3b_hurt\": 0.73,\n366\t      \"capacity_ratio_at_rebound\": 0.31,\n367\t      \"capacity_ratio_at_monotonic_1_3b\": 0.12,\n368\t      \"scale_contrast_narrative\": \"1.3B 有足够容量同时支持 recurrence core 和 attention，两者互补； 340M 在高 attention ratio 时两者竞争参数预算，形成 capacity bottleneck。\\n\",\n369\t      \"training_tokens_confound_ruled_out\": true,\n370\t      \"confound_evidence\": \"per-example rebound pattern matches capacity prediction, not token-count prediction\"\n371\t    },\n372\t    \"tables\": [\n373\t      {\n374\t        \"name\": \"Table 6: 340M rebound characterization\",\n375\t        \"columns\": [\n376\t          \"Metric\",\n377\t          \"340M ratio=6\",\n378\t          \"340M ratio=8 (rebound)\",\n379\t          \"1.3B ratio=8\",\n380\t          \"Interpretation\"\n381\t        ],\n382\t        \"rows\": [\n383\t          [\n384\t            \"Cross-arch std\",\n385\t            \"0.009\",\n386\t            \"0.014\",\n387\t            \"0.006\",\n388\t            \"340M rebounds, 1.3B continues declining\"\n389\t          ],\n390\t          [\n391\t            \"Attention param ratio\",\n392\t            \"0.23\",\n393\t            \"0.31\",\n394\t            \"0.12\",\n395\t            \"340M capacity squeeze at ratio=8\"\n396\t          ],\n397\t          [\n398\t            \"Rebound samples (became incorrect)\",\n399\t            \"—\",\n400\t            \"412\",\n401\t            \"0 (still correct)\",\n402\t            \"Capacity bottleneck\"\n403\t          ],\n404\t          [\n405\t            \"Rebound sample features\",\n406\t            \"—\",\n407\t            \"Long context + high-freq tokens\",\n408\t            \"N/A\",\n409\t            \"Needs strong recurrence\"\n410\t          ]\n411\t        ]\n412\t      }\n413\t    ],\n414\t    \"figures\": [],\n415\t    \"analysis\": \"Capacity bottleneck 机制清晰且有 falsifiable prediction（如果是 capacity 问题， 则 rebound samples 应集中在 recurrence-demanding 特征上——已验证）。排除了 training token confound。340M vs 1.3B 的对比从 aggregate 观察（\\\"scale matters\\\"） 升级为 mechanistic explanation（\\\"sufficient capacity is prerequisite for attention to complement rather than compete with recurrence\\\"）。这为 Claim 2 提供了 two-scale 情况下能达到的最强叙事。\\n\\n\\n340M 模型总参数有限，attention layer 的参数开销在 ratio=8 时占比达到 ~31%， 远高于 1.3B 同 ratio 时的 ~12%。这种参数预算竞争导致 recurrence core 的 effective capacity 下降。具体表现为：340M 在 ratio=8 时有 412 个 sample 从 correct 变为 incorrect（这些 sample 在 ratio=6 时还是 correct），其中 73% 在 1.3B ratio=8 时仍然 correct——说明问题在于 capacity 而非 attention 本身的 负面效应。训练 token 数量差异（20B vs 100B）作为 confound 被排除：如果是 token count 导致，则 rebound 应该在所有 sample 上均匀分布；但实际 rebound 集中在 需要 strong recurrence（长距离依赖 + 高 token frequency）的 sample 上， 符合 capacity bottleneck 预测而非 token-count 预测。\\n\"\n416\t  },\n417\t  {\n418\t    \"name\": \"Statistical robustness framework\",\n419\t    \"description\": \"Bootstrap CI、多重比较校正、GDN 排除敏感性分析、effect size 报告。\\n\",\n420\t    \"results\": {\n421\t      \"lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_ci_pct\": [\n422\t        72,\n423\t        86\n424\t      ],\n425\t      \"lambada_std_reduction_point\": 79,\n426\t      \"lambada_rho_bootstrap_ci\": [\n427\t        -1.0,\n428\t        -0.9\n429\t      ],\n430\t      \"lambada_rho_point\": -1.0,\n431\t      \"bonferroni_corrected_lambada_p\": 0.05,\n432\t      \"fdr_corrected_lambada_p\": 0.025,\n433\t      \"lambada_survives_correction\": true,\n434\t      \"arc_easy_survives_correction\": false,\n435\t      \"gdn_excluded_lambada_rho\": -1.0,\n436\t      \"gdn_excluded_std_reduction\": 74,\n437\t      \"gdn_excluded_claim1_survives\": true,\n438\t      \"gdn_excluded_claim2_survives\": true,\n439\t      \"gdn_excluded_claim3_survives\": true,\n440\t      \"claims_surviving_gdn_exclusion\": 3,\n441\t      \"cohens_d_lambada_convergence\": 1.84,\n442\t      \"eta_squared_attention_ratio_effect\": 0.67,\n443\t      \"bootstrap_iterations\": 10000\n444\t    },\n445\t    \"tables\": [\n446\t      {\n447\t        \"name\": \"Table 7: Bootstrap confidence intervals\",\n448\t        \"columns\": [\n449\t          \"Metric\",\n450\t          \"Point estimate\",\n451\t          \"Bootstrap 95% CI\",\n452\t          \"Survives Bonferroni?\"\n453\t        ],\n454\t        \"rows\": [\n455\t          [\n456\t            \"LAMBADA std reduction %\",\n457\t            \"79%\",\n458\t            \"[72%, 86%]\",\n459\t            \"Yes\"\n460\t          ],\n461\t          [\n462\t            \"LAMBADA ρ\",\n463\t            \"-1.00\",\n464\t            \"[-1.00, -0.90]\",\n465\t            \"Yes\"\n466\t          ],\n467\t          [\n468\t            \"ARC-Easy ρ\",\n469\t            \"-0.85\",\n470\t            \"[-1.00, -0.50]\",\n471\t            \"No (suggestive)\"\n472\t          ],\n473\t          [\n474\t            \"Cross-arch Jaccard mean\",\n475\t            \"0.06\",\n476\t            \"[0.03, 0.09]\",\n477\t            \"N/A\"\n478\t          ]\n479\t        ]\n480\t      },\n481\t      {\n482\t        \"name\": \"Table 7b: GDN exclusion sensitivity\",\n483\t        \"columns\": [\n484\t          \"Claim\",\n485\t          \"With GDN\",\n486\t          \"Without GDN\",\n487\t          \"Survives?\"\n488\t        ],\n489\t        \"rows\": [\n490\t          [\n491\t            \"Claim 1 (task-specific convergence)\",\n492\t            \"ρ=-1.0, 79% reduction\",\n493\t            \"ρ=-1.0, 74% reduction\",\n494\t            \"Yes\"\n495\t          ],\n496\t          [\n497\t            \"Claim 2 (scale-dependent)\",\n498\t            \"340M partial, 1.3B complete\",\n499\t            \"Same pattern (RetNet/HGRN2/Mamba2)\",\n500\t            \"Yes\"\n501\t          ],\n502\t          [\n503\t            \"Claim 3 (arch-specific mechanism)\",\n504\t            \"Jaccard=0.06, 3 profiles\",\n505\t            \"Jaccard=0.08, 2+1 profiles\",\n506\t            \"Yes\"\n507\t          ]\n508\t        ]\n509\t      }\n510\t    ],\n511\t    \"figures\": [],\n512\t    \"analysis\": \"统计框架完整且所有核心 claim 通过 robustness check。GDN exclusion 是最关键的 sensitivity test（因为 GDN 有 D004 confound），三条 claim 均成立。LAMBADA 在 多重比较后仍显著是 best tier 的关键指标——Bonferroni 边界通过（p=0.0083 for 6 tests, observed p=0.0083）。Bootstrap CI 范围 [72%, 86%] 完全落在 best tier 指标范围 [70, 88] 内。\\n\\n\\nLAMBADA 的 convergence effect size 极大（Cohen's d=1.84），Bootstrap 10000 次 迭代后 CI [72%, 86%] 不跨零，即使取下界 72% 仍是强效应。Bonferroni 校正 （6 benchmarks → α=0.0083）后 LAMBADA 仍显著（原始 p=0.0083，校正后刚好 在边界但通过），FDR 校正更宽松（p=0.025）。ARC-Easy 因 power 不足在 Bonferroni 后不显著（p=0.117），但在 continuous spectrum 叙事中作为\\\"suggestive\\\"仍有价值。 GDN 排除后（n=2 架构 + Mamba2），LAMBADA ρ 保持 -1.0（RetNet 和 HGRN2 本身就 呈现完美单调收敛），std reduction 从 79% 降至 74%（因样本量减少，估计略保守）， 但三条 claim 均成立。这是因为 GDN 虽有 D004 confound，但 convergence 不依赖 GDN—— 任意两个架构之间都呈现收敛。Claim 3 在 GDN 排除后也成立因为 RetNet vs HGRN2 的 Jaccard 仅 0.08，且 effect direction 相反（RetNet hurt, HGRN2 helped）。\\n\"\n513\t  },\n514\t  {\n515\t    \"name\": \"Wang et al. explicit differentiation\",\n516\t    \"description\": \"逐点对比 Wang et al. 的 exact statements 与我们的分析，建立清晰的四点增量。\\n\",\n517\t    \"results\": {\n518\t      \"wang_convergence_mentions\": 3,\n519\t      \"wang_quantitative_convergence\": 0,\n520\t      \"wang_per_example_analysis\": 0,\n521\t      \"wang_scale_dependent_analysis\": 0,\n522\t      \"wang_mechanistic_analysis\": 0,\n523\t      \"differentiation_points\": 4,\n524\t      \"wang_exact_quotes_extracted\": 3\n525\t    },\n526\t    \"tables\": [\n527\t      {\n528\t        \"name\": \"Table 8: Systematic comparison with Wang et al. (2025)\",\n529\t        \"columns\": [\n530\t          \"Analysis dimension\",\n531\t          \"Wang et al.\",\n532\t          \"This work\"\n533\t        ],\n534\t        \"rows\": [\n535\t          [\n536\t            \"Cross-arch convergence quantification\",\n537\t            \"Qualitative ('gap narrows')\",\n538\t            \"Spearman ρ=-1.0, std reduction 79%, bootstrap CI\"\n539\t          ],\n540\t          [\n541\t            \"Per-example mechanism\",\n542\t            \"Not analyzed\",\n543\t            \"Jaccard<0.10, architecture-specific helped/hurt subsets\"\n544\t          ],\n545\t          [\n546\t            \"Scale dependency\",\n547\t            \"Not analyzed\",\n548\t            \"Binary contrast: 340M partial (rebound) vs 1.3B complete, capacity bottleneck mechanism\"\n549\t          ],\n550\t          [\n551\t            \"Task-specificity\",\n552\t            \"Not analyzed\",\n553\t            \"Continuous retrieval-demand spectrum, 6 benchmarks, dose-response curve\"\n554\t          ]\n555\t        ]\n556\t      }\n557\t    ],\n558\t    \"figures\": [],\n559\t    \"analysis\": \"四点 differentiation 清晰且无重叠。我们使用 Wang et al. 的 model zoo（proper attribution）但提供了他们完全没有的分析维度。这回应 Reviewer Risk 4 和 Concern E， 将我们的贡献从\\\"also studied convergence\\\"提升到\\\"discovered and characterized a phenomenon they only glimpsed qualitatively\\\"。\\n\\n\\nWang et al. 的论文是 model zoo paper，核心贡献是训练并开源 72 个模型。他们对 convergence 的提及限于 qualitative observations（如 \\\"performance gap narrows with more attention layers\\\"），没有 (a) 计算 cross-arch std trajectories 或 Spearman ρ，(b) 做 per-example analysis，(c) 分析 scale dependency of convergence， (d) 提供 mechanistic explanation。我们的增量恰好是他们没做的四件事。这四点 differentiation 在 paper 中以 explicit side-by-side table 呈现，让 reviewer 一目了然。\\n\"\n560\t  },\n561\t  {\n562\t    \"name\": \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\",\n563\t    \"description\": \"在 LAMBADA 上，以 attention ratio 为 x 轴，同时绘制 aggregate convergence（cross-arch std） 和 per-example divergence（Jaccard, net effect asymmetry），展示 paradox 的共同演化。\\n\",\n564\t    \"results\": {\n565\t      \"convergence_divergence_correlation\": -0.94,\n566\t      \"convergence_divergence_p\": 0.005,\n567\t      \"paradox_strengthens_with_attention\": true,\n568\t      \"jaccard_at_ratio_0\": \"N/A (no attention effect)\",\n569\t      \"jaccard_at_ratio_1\": 0.08,\n570\t      \"jaccard_at_ratio_6\": 0.06,\n571\t      \"jaccard_at_ratio_24\": 0.04,\n572\t      \"std_at_ratio_0\": 0.024,\n573\t      \"std_at_ratio_24\": 0.005,\n574\t      \"net_effect_asymmetry_gdn\": -0.12,\n575\t      \"net_effect_asymmetry_retnet\": -0.08,\n576\t      \"net_effect_asymmetry_hgrn2\": 0.11\n577\t    },\n578\t    \"tables\": [\n579\t      {\n580\t        \"name\": \"Table 9: Convergence-divergence co-evolution by attention ratio\",\n581\t        \"columns\": [\n582\t          \"Attention ratio\",\n583\t          \"Cross-arch std\",\n584\t          \"Jaccard (mean pairwise)\",\n585\t          \"GDN net effect\",\n586\t          \"RetNet net effect\",\n587\t          \"HGRN2 net effect\"\n588\t        ],\n589\t        \"rows\": [\n590\t          [\n591\t            \"0 (pure recurrent)\",\n592\t            \"0.024\",\n593\t            \"—\",\n594\t            \"0.00\",\n595\t            \"0.00\",\n596\t            \"0.00\"\n597\t          ],\n598\t          [\n599\t            \"1\",\n600\t            \"0.018\",\n601\t            \"0.08\",\n602\t            \"-0.03\",\n603\t            \"-0.02\",\n604\t            \"+0.03\"\n605\t          ],\n606\t          [\n607\t            \"3\",\n608\t            \"0.012\",\n609\t            \"0.07\",\n610\t            \"-0.06\",\n611\t            \"-0.04\",\n612\t            \"+0.06\"\n613\t          ],\n614\t          [\n615\t            \"6\",\n616\t            \"0.008\",\n617\t            \"0.06\",\n618\t            \"-0.09\",\n619\t            \"-0.06\",\n620\t            \"+0.08\"\n621\t          ],\n622\t          [\n623\t            \"8\",\n624\t            \"0.007\",\n625\t            \"0.05\",\n626\t            \"-0.10\",\n627\t            \"-0.07\",\n628\t            \"+0.10\"\n629\t          ],\n630\t          [\n631\t            \"24\",\n632\t            \"0.005\",\n633\t            \"0.04\",\n634\t            \"-0.12\",\n635\t            \"-0.08\",\n636\t            \"+0.11\"\n637\t          ]\n638\t        ]\n639\t      }\n640\t    ],\n641\t    \"figures\": [],\n642\t    \"analysis\": \"Convergence-divergence co-evolution（r=-0.94, p=0.005）是 paper 的 hero result， 直接可视化了 title 中的 \\\"Equalizer Paradox\\\"。这不是一个偶然发现，而是 attention 作为\\\"equalizer\\\"的内在机制：它通过在不同架构上做不同的事来实现 aggregate 趋同。 Net effect asymmetry 的对称性（GDN/RetNet hurt, HGRN2 helped, 幅度近似）表明 convergence 不是某个架构\\\"被拉上来\\\"，而是所有架构\\\"被推向中间\\\"——这与 paper title \\\"Equalizer\\\" 的隐喻完美对应。此图应作为 paper 的 Figure 1 或 graphical abstract。\\n\\n随着 attention ratio 增加，aggregate convergence 增强（std 从 0.024 降到 0.005） 而 per-example divergence 也增强（Jaccard 从 0.08 降到 0.04，意味着 helped/hurt subsets 越来越不重叠）。两者负相关（r=-0.94）是 paradox 的数学必然：当各架构 的 aggregate 趋同但 per-example effect magnitude 增大时，唯一的解释是各架构在 不同 sample 上做了更大幅度的\\\"互补性\\\"调整。更多 attention = 更强的补偿效应 = aggregate 更趋同 + per-example 更 divergent。Net effect asymmetry（GDN 和 RetNet net negative, HGRN2 net positive）在所有 attention ratio 保持方向一致但幅度 随 ratio 增大，呈现对称但相反的效应——这就是 \\\"equalizer paradox\\\" 的核心可视化。\\n\"\n643\t  }\n644\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e458f2f1-96ec-4b1e-abae-2d80d2354b5b","uuid":"f82fe115-85c7-48ef-ba76-45bbc94c43a1","timestamp":"2026-05-19T13:28:20.951Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/entrainment_gated_ft/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260519T131014/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Task-specificity characterization of equalizer effect\",\n    \"description\": \"对 6 个 benchmark 计算 1.3B 下各 attention ratio 的 cross-architecture std， 建立 convergence strength（Spearman ρ）与 retrieval demand 的连续关系。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"lambada_rho\": -1.0,\n      \"lambada_std_reduction_pct\": 79,\n      \"arc_easy_rho\": -0.7,\n      \"arc_challenge_rho\": -0.3,\n      \"hellaswag_rho\": -0.1,\n      \"winogrande_rho\": 0.05,\n      \"mmlu_rho\": 0.1,\n      \"benchmarks_with_rho_below_neg05\": 2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: Cross-architecture convergence by benchmark\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Retrieval Demand (BIG-bench)\",\n          \"ρ (std vs attn ratio)\",\n          \"p-value (permutation)\",\n          \"Std at ratio=0\",\n          \"Std at ratio=24\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LAMBADA\",\n            \"High\",\n            \"-1.00\",\n            \"0.0083\",\n            \"0.024\",\n            \"0.005\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Easy\",\n            \"Medium-High\",\n            \"-0.70\",\n            \"0.117\",\n            \"0.031\",\n            \"0.018\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n            \"Medium\",\n            \"-0.30\",\n            \"0.347\",\n            \"0.022\",\n            \"0.019\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            \"Low\",\n            \"-0.10\",\n            \"0.782\",\n            \"0.018\",\n            \"0.017\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"WinoGrande\",\n            \"Low-Medium\",\n            \"0.05\",\n            \"0.912\",\n            \"0.015\",\n            \"0.016\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"Low\",\n            \"0.10\",\n            \"0.782\",\n            \"0.028\",\n            \"0.027\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Continuous retrieval-demand spectrum 成立。避免了 binary retrieval/reasoning 分类的 post-hoc cherry-picking 风险。BIG-bench taxonomy 提供外部锚定。LAMBADA + ARC-Easy 两个锚点形成梯度，其余 benchmark 填充低端。Reviewer Concern B 通过 dose-response framing 化解。\\n\\n\\nLAMBADA 是纯 last-word retrieval 任务，attention 的 key-value lookup 机制天然对齐 这类需求，因此跨架构方差压缩最彻底（ρ=-1.0）。ARC-Easy 含大量事实检索型题目， attention 部分有效（ρ=-0.7）。HellaSwag/WinoGrande/MMLU 以推理、常识、世界知识为主， attention 的收敛作用被 recurrence core 的架构差异主导，ρ 趋近零。这形成了以 retrieval demand 为横轴的 dose-response 曲线，两个显著锚点（LAMBADA + ARC-Easy）足以建立 continuous spectrum 的可信度。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"对 1.3B 模型（GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 × 5 attention ratios）和 10×340M 模型重新运行 lm-eval --log_samples，收集 HellaSwag、ARC-Easy、ARC-Challenge 的 per-example 数据。 分析 per-example 层面是否存在 convergence 或 task-specific divergence。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"hellaswag_per_example_convergence\": false,\n      \"hellaswag_per_example_pattern\": \"systematic architecture-specific, not random noise\",\n      \"arc_easy_per_example_convergence\": true,\n      \"arc_easy_rho_after_per_example\": -0.85,\n      \"arc_easy_jaccard_pairwise\": 0.12,\n      \"arc_challenge_per_example_convergence\": false,\n      \"arc_challenge_per_example_pattern\": \"weak, architecture-independent noise\",\n      \"models_evaluated\": 23,\n      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 18\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2: Per-example convergence metrics by benchmark\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"N samples\",\n          \"Aggregate ρ\",\n          \"Per-example ρ (filtered)\",\n          \"Jaccard (pairwise mean)\",\n          \"Pattern type\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LAMBADA\",\n            \"5153\",\n            \"-1.00\",\n            \"-1.00\",\n            \"0.06\",\n            \"Architecture-specific convergence\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Easy\",\n            \"2376\",\n            \"-0.70\",\n            \"-0.85\",\n            \"0.12\",\n            \"Retrieval-subset convergence\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n            \"1172\",\n            \"-0.30\",\n            \"-0.25\",\n            \"0.31\",\n            \"No systematic pattern\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            \"10042\",\n            \"-0.10\",\n            \"-0.08\",\n            \"0.22\",\n            \"Systematic but non-converging\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-002 的 best 结果是双重确认：(1) HellaSwag/ARC-C 在 per-example 层面确认非收敛， 升级 task-specificity 从\\\"aggregate insignificant\\\"到\\\"per-example confirmed non-converging\\\"； (2) ARC-Easy 在去噪后 ρ 加强至 -0.85，成为第二个强锚点。Continuous spectrum 从 单点（LAMBADA）变为双锚点梯度，极大加强 Claim 1。\\n\\n\\nHellaSwag 在 aggregate 层面无收敛（ρ=-0.1），per-example 分析确认这不是 power 问题而是 真阴性——attention 在不同架构上改变不同 sample 的正确率，但这些变化是 systematic architecture-specific（每个架构有自己稳定的 helped/hurt subset），而非 random noise。 这说明 attention 在推理任务上\\\"做了事\\\"但没有跨架构趋同。ARC-Easy 在 per-example 层面 发现 attention 确实压缩了跨架构差异：对 retrieval-heavy 子题（事实召回型），三个架构的 正确率 variance 下降；对 reasoning-heavy 子题则无变化。这将 aggregate ρ 从 -0.70 加强至 -0.85（通过去除 reasoning 子题噪声）。ARC-Easy 成为 continuous spectrum 的 第二个强锚点。ARC-Challenge 因推理占比高，per-example 无系统模式。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Helped/hurt sample characterization\",\n    \"description\": \"对 LAMBADA 上各架构的 helped/hurt samples 计算 token frequency、context length、 last-sentence perplexity、domain 分布。测试 feature 是否区分 helped/hurt，且跨架构 feature profile 是否不同。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_features_significant_p001\": 3,\n      \"best_feature\": \"target_token_frequency\",\n      \"best_feature_p\": 2.5e-05,\n      \"second_feature\": \"context_length\",\n      \"second_feature_p\": 0.00031,\n      \"third_feature\": \"last_sentence_perplexity\",\n      \"third_feature_p\": 0.00087,\n      \"gdn_profile\": \"helped on rare tokens + long contexts\",\n      \"retnet_profile\": \"helped on high-perplexity last sentences\",\n      \"hgrn2_profile\": \"helped broadly but strongest on medium-frequency tokens\",\n      \"cross_arch_profile_difference_p\": 0.0003,\n      \"effect_size_cohens_d_best\": 0.72\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 3: Feature importance for helped/hurt classification by architecture\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Feature\",\n          \"GDN (AUC)\",\n          \"RetNet (AUC)\",\n          \"HGRN2 (AUC)\",\n          \"Overall p-value\",\n          \"Cross-arch difference p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Target token freq (log rank)\",\n            \"0.71\",\n            \"0.58\",\n            \"0.64\",\n            \"2.5e-05\",\n            \"0.0012\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Context length (tokens)\",\n            \"0.67\",\n            \"0.55\",\n            \"0.57\",\n            \"3.1e-04\",\n            \"0.0089\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Last-sentence perplexity\",\n            \"0.56\",\n            \"0.69\",\n            \"0.61\",\n            \"8.7e-04\",\n            \"0.0003\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Domain (topic entropy)\",\n            \"0.54\",\n            \"0.53\",\n            \"0.55\",\n            \"0.042\",\n            \"0.31\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"3 个 feature 在 p<0.001 水平显著区分 helped/hurt，且跨架构 profile 统计显著不同。 这为 Claim 3（architecture-specific mechanism）提供了 feature-level 解释：不是抽象的 \\\"不同 sample\\\"，而是\\\"不同语言学特征的 sample\\\"。Feature profile 差异直接映射到各架构 recurrence core 的已知机制特性（delta rule → rare token recall; exponential decay → local disambiguation; hierarchical gating → multi-scale memory）。\\n\\n\\nGatedDeltaNet 的 delta rule 机制擅长 associative recall，attention 补充的是对 rare token 的 precise retrieval（delta rule 对 rare token 的 update 不够精确）， 因此 GDN helped samples 集中在 rare token + long context（需要远距离检索）。RetNet 的 exponential decay 使其对 last sentence 内的局部信息较强，attention 补充的是 high-perplexity last sentence 中的 disambiguation（decay 无法区分多个候选），因此 RetNet helped samples 集中在 high-perplexity last sentence。HGRN2 的 hierarchical gating 提供多尺度记忆但对 token frequency 有 sweet spot，attention 拓宽了这个 sweet spot。三种架构的 feature profile 统计显著不同（p<0.001），这直接解释了为什么 Jaccard overlap 低——它们被 attention 帮助的 sample 具有不同的语言学特征。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\",\n    \"description\": \"从 h3-1 配置的三个架构提取 attention weight，分析 attention pattern 与 per-example helped/hurt identity 的相关性，以及跨架构 attention pattern 的相似度。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"attention_per_example_correlation_gdn\": 0.52,\n      \"attention_per_example_correlation_retnet\": 0.61,\n      \"attention_per_example_correlation_hgrn2\": 0.48,\n      \"attention_per_example_correlation_mean\": 0.54,\n      \"cross_arch_attention_similarity\": 0.23,\n      \"gdn_attention_focus\": \"distributed over long-range context tokens\",\n      \"retnet_attention_focus\": \"concentrated on last-sentence tokens\",\n      \"hgrn2_attention_focus\": \"hierarchical — split between local and mid-range\",\n      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 3.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 4: Attention pattern analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Architecture\",\n          \"Attention focus\",\n          \"Corr with helped/hurt\",\n          \"p-value\",\n          \"Mean entropy\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GDN\",\n            \"Long-range distributed\",\n            \"0.52\",\n            \"1.2e-04\",\n            \"3.41\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RetNet\",\n            \"Last-sentence concentrated\",\n            \"0.61\",\n            \"8.7e-06\",\n            \"2.18\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HGRN2\",\n            \"Hierarchical split\",\n            \"0.48\",\n            \"4.3e-04\",\n            \"2.89\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 4b: Cross-architecture attention similarity (cosine)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Pair\",\n          \"Mean cosine sim\",\n          \"Significance vs random baseline\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GDN-RetNet\",\n            \"0.19\",\n            \"p<0.001 (below random)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GDN-HGRN2\",\n            \"0.27\",\n            \"p=0.003 (below random)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RetNet-HGRN2\",\n            \"0.24\",\n            \"p=0.001 (below random)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Mean correlation 0.54（range 0.48–0.61）超过 pass_fail 阈值 0.4，提供了 mechanistic evidence 的第二根支柱。与 exp-003 的 feature 分析合在一起，形成完整因果链： recurrence core 特性 → attention 学到补偿性 pattern → 补偿作用在不同语言学特征 的 sample 上生效 → 各架构 aggregate 性能趋同但 per-example 效果不重叠。 这回应 Reviewer Concern C（\\\"no causal mechanism\\\"），从 correlation 升级到 directed mechanistic narrative。\\n\\n\\nAttention layer 在不同 recurrence backbone 上学到了不同的 attention pattern，因为 它在补偿各架构 recurrence core 的不同弱点。GDN 的 delta rule 已经做了一定的 associative memory，attention 学会关注 long-range context（补充 delta rule 的 远距离衰减）。RetNet 的 exponential decay 快速遗忘远距离信息，attention 集中在 last-sentence 内做 disambiguation（因为 RetNet 对近距离信息已经较强）。HGRN2 的 hierarchical gating 在多个尺度上保留信息但每个尺度都不够精确，attention 学会 hierarchical 分配。这些不同的 attention pattern 与 helped/hurt sample 的对应关系 ≥0.4（最高 RetNet 0.61），因为 attention 的\\\"关注什么\\\"直接决定了\\\"帮助哪些 sample\\\"。 跨架构 attention similarity 仅 0.23，远低于随机基线 0.5，这是 mechanistic evidence 的核心：同样的 attention 架构在不同 recurrence backbone 上学到了完全不同的行为。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Architecture expansion check\",\n    \"description\": \"搜索 Wang et al. model zoo 及其他来源，找到额外的 hybrid 架构（Mamba hybrid 等）， 在 LAMBADA 上评估收敛模式是否复现。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"additional_architectures_found\": 1,\n      \"architecture_name\": \"Mamba2-Attn hybrid (from community reproduction)\",\n      \"architecture_type\": \"selective state space + attention\",\n      \"lambada_convergence_confirmed\": true,\n      \"mamba2_rho\": -0.9,\n      \"mamba2_std_reduction_pct\": 71,\n      \"mamba2_jaccard_with_others\": 0.05,\n      \"total_architectures_tested\": 4,\n      \"gpu_hours_actual\": 5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 5: Architecture expansion — convergence on LAMBADA\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Architecture\",\n          \"Recurrence type\",\n          \"ρ (std vs attn ratio)\",\n          \"Std reduction %\",\n          \"Jaccard with GDN\",\n          \"Jaccard with RetNet\",\n          \"Jaccard with HGRN2\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GDN\",\n            \"Gated delta rule\",\n            \"-1.00\",\n            \"79%\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"0.06\",\n            \"0.04\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RetNet\",\n            \"Linear attn + exp decay\",\n            \"-1.00\",\n            \"79%\",\n            \"0.06\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"0.08\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HGRN2\",\n            \"Hierarchical gating\",\n            \"-1.00\",\n            \"79%\",\n            \"0.04\",\n            \"0.08\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mamba2-Attn\",\n            \"Selective state space\",\n            \"-0.90\",\n            \"71%\",\n            \"0.05\",\n            \"0.04\",\n            \"0.07\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Mamba2-Attn 的加入将 architectures_tested 从 3 提升到 4，覆盖了四种不同的 recurrence mechanism。收敛模式复现（ρ=-0.90, std reduction 71%），且 Jaccard 保持低水平， 说明 equalizer effect 不是三个特定架构的巧合，而是 attention + any recurrence 的 通用现象。这是 generalization evidence 的最佳结果，直接提升论文的 impact 和 reviewer 的信任度。\\n\\n\\nMamba2 的 selective state space mechanism 与 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 的 linear recurrence 不同（selection mechanism vs gating/delta rule/exponential decay），但 attention 的补偿效应仍然成立：Mamba2 的 state selection 对某类 retrieval pattern 较弱， attention 补充后 aggregate 性能趋同。ρ=-0.90（略弱于 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 的 -1.0） 可能因为 Mamba2 hybrid 的 attention 集成方式略有不同（interleaved vs stacked）， 但趋势一致。Jaccard 0.05 表明 Mamba2 的 helped/hurt subset 与其他三个架构同样 不重叠，进一步支持 architecture-specific mechanism。n=4 架构使得 Reviewer Concern D （\\\"n=3 too few\\\"）大幅缓解。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"深入分析 340M 在 attn=8 时的非单调 rebound。与 1.3B 同 attention ratio 做 per-example 对比，识别 diverge 的 sample 并 characterize rebound 机制。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rebound_mechanism\": \"capacity bottleneck\",\n      \"rebound_explanation\": \"340M 在 attn ratio=8 时，attention 参数占总参数比例过高（~30%）， 压缩了 recurrence core 的有效容量。Recurrence core 性能下降的 sample 与 attention 新帮助的 sample 不完全重叠，导致 aggregate std 回升。\\n\",\n      \"rebound_samples_n\": 412,\n      \"rebound_samples_overlap_with_1_3b_hurt\": 0.73,\n      \"capacity_ratio_at_rebound\": 0.31,\n      \"capacity_ratio_at_monotonic_1_3b\": 0.12,\n      \"scale_contrast_narrative\": \"1.3B 有足够容量同时支持 recurrence core 和 attention，两者互补； 340M 在高 attention ratio 时两者竞争参数预算，形成 capacity bottleneck。\\n\",\n      \"training_tokens_confound_ruled_out\": true,\n      \"confound_evidence\": \"per-example rebound pattern matches capacity prediction, not token-count prediction\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 6: 340M rebound characterization\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"340M ratio=6\",\n          \"340M ratio=8 (rebound)\",\n          \"1.3B ratio=8\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Cross-arch std\",\n            \"0.009\",\n            \"0.014\",\n            \"0.006\",\n            \"340M rebounds, 1.3B continues declining\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Attention param ratio\",\n            \"0.23\",\n            \"0.31\",\n            \"0.12\",\n            \"340M capacity squeeze at ratio=8\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Rebound samples (became incorrect)\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"412\",\n            \"0 (still correct)\",\n            \"Capacity bottleneck\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Rebound sample features\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"Long context + high-freq tokens\",\n            \"N/A\",\n            \"Needs strong recurrence\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Capacity bottleneck 机制清晰且有 falsifiable prediction（如果是 capacity 问题， 则 rebound samples 应集中在 recurrence-demanding 特征上——已验证）。排除了 training token confound。340M vs 1.3B 的对比从 aggregate 观察（\\\"scale matters\\\"） 升级为 mechanistic explanation（\\\"sufficient capacity is prerequisite for attention to complement rather than compete with recurrence\\\"）。这为 Claim 2 提供了 two-scale 情况下能达到的最强叙事。\\n\\n\\n340M 模型总参数有限，attention layer 的参数开销在 ratio=8 时占比达到 ~31%， 远高于 1.3B 同 ratio 时的 ~12%。这种参数预算竞争导致 recurrence core 的 effective capacity 下降。具体表现为：340M 在 ratio=8 时有 412 个 sample 从 correct 变为 incorrect（这些 sample 在 ratio=6 时还是 correct），其中 73% 在 1.3B ratio=8 时仍然 correct——说明问题在于 capacity 而非 attention 本身的 负面效应。训练 token 数量差异（20B vs 100B）作为 confound 被排除：如果是 token count 导致，则 rebound 应该在所有 sample 上均匀分布；但实际 rebound 集中在 需要 strong recurrence（长距离依赖 + 高 token frequency）的 sample 上， 符合 capacity bottleneck 预测而非 token-count 预测。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Statistical robustness framework\",\n    \"description\": \"Bootstrap CI、多重比较校正、GDN 排除敏感性分析、effect size 报告。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"lambada_std_reduction_bootstrap_ci_pct\": [\n        72,\n        86\n      ],\n      \"lambada_std_reduction_point\": 79,\n      \"lambada_rho_bootstrap_ci\": [\n        -1.0,\n        -0.9\n      ],\n      \"lambada_rho_point\": -1.0,\n      \"bonferroni_corrected_lambada_p\": 0.05,\n      \"fdr_corrected_lambada_p\": 0.025,\n      \"lambada_survives_correction\": true,\n      \"arc_easy_survives_correction\": false,\n      \"gdn_excluded_lambada_rho\": -1.0,\n      \"gdn_excluded_std_reduction\": 74,\n      \"gdn_excluded_claim1_survives\": true,\n      \"gdn_excluded_claim2_survives\": true,\n      \"gdn_excluded_claim3_survives\": true,\n      \"claims_surviving_gdn_exclusion\": 3,\n      \"cohens_d_lambada_convergence\": 1.84,\n      \"eta_squared_attention_ratio_effect\": 0.67,\n      \"bootstrap_iterations\": 10000\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 7: Bootstrap confidence intervals\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Point estimate\",\n          \"Bootstrap 95% CI\",\n          \"Survives Bonferroni?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LAMBADA std reduction %\",\n            \"79%\",\n            \"[72%, 86%]\",\n            \"Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LAMBADA ρ\",\n            \"-1.00\",\n            \"[-1.00, -0.90]\",\n            \"Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Easy ρ\",\n            \"-0.85\",\n            \"[-1.00, -0.50]\",\n            \"No (suggestive)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cross-arch Jaccard mean\",\n            \"0.06\",\n            \"[0.03, 0.09]\",\n            \"N/A\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 7b: GDN exclusion sensitivity\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Claim\",\n          \"With GDN\",\n          \"Without GDN\",\n          \"Survives?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Claim 1 (task-specific convergence)\",\n            \"ρ=-1.0, 79% reduction\",\n            \"ρ=-1.0, 74% reduction\",\n            \"Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claim 2 (scale-dependent)\",\n            \"340M partial, 1.3B complete\",\n            \"Same pattern (RetNet/HGRN2/Mamba2)\",\n            \"Yes\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claim 3 (arch-specific mechanism)\",\n            \"Jaccard=0.06, 3 profiles\",\n            \"Jaccard=0.08, 2+1 profiles\",\n            \"Yes\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"统计框架完整且所有核心 claim 通过 robustness check。GDN exclusion 是最关键的 sensitivity test（因为 GDN 有 D004 confound），三条 claim 均成立。LAMBADA 在 多重比较后仍显著是 best tier 的关键指标——Bonferroni 边界通过（p=0.0083 for 6 tests, observed p=0.0083）。Bootstrap CI 范围 [72%, 86%] 完全落在 best tier 指标范围 [70, 88] 内。\\n\\n\\nLAMBADA 的 convergence effect size 极大（Cohen's d=1.84），Bootstrap 10000 次 迭代后 CI [72%, 86%] 不跨零，即使取下界 72% 仍是强效应。Bonferroni 校正 （6 benchmarks → α=0.0083）后 LAMBADA 仍显著（原始 p=0.0083，校正后刚好 在边界但通过），FDR 校正更宽松（p=0.025）。ARC-Easy 因 power 不足在 Bonferroni 后不显著（p=0.117），但在 continuous spectrum 叙事中作为\\\"suggestive\\\"仍有价值。 GDN 排除后（n=2 架构 + Mamba2），LAMBADA ρ 保持 -1.0（RetNet 和 HGRN2 本身就 呈现完美单调收敛），std reduction 从 79% 降至 74%（因样本量减少，估计略保守）， 但三条 claim 均成立。这是因为 GDN 虽有 D004 confound，但 convergence 不依赖 GDN—— 任意两个架构之间都呈现收敛。Claim 3 在 GDN 排除后也成立因为 RetNet vs HGRN2 的 Jaccard 仅 0.08，且 effect direction 相反（RetNet hurt, HGRN2 helped）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Wang et al. explicit differentiation\",\n    \"description\": \"逐点对比 Wang et al. 的 exact statements 与我们的分析，建立清晰的四点增量。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"wang_convergence_mentions\": 3,\n      \"wang_quantitative_convergence\": 0,\n      \"wang_per_example_analysis\": 0,\n      \"wang_scale_dependent_analysis\": 0,\n      \"wang_mechanistic_analysis\": 0,\n      \"differentiation_points\": 4,\n      \"wang_exact_quotes_extracted\": 3\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 8: Systematic comparison with Wang et al. (2025)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Analysis dimension\",\n          \"Wang et al.\",\n          \"This work\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Cross-arch convergence quantification\",\n            \"Qualitative ('gap narrows')\",\n            \"Spearman ρ=-1.0, std reduction 79%, bootstrap CI\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Per-example mechanism\",\n            \"Not analyzed\",\n            \"Jaccard<0.10, architecture-specific helped/hurt subsets\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Scale dependency\",\n            \"Not analyzed\",\n            \"Binary contrast: 340M partial (rebound) vs 1.3B complete, capacity bottleneck mechanism\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Task-specificity\",\n            \"Not analyzed\",\n            \"Continuous retrieval-demand spectrum, 6 benchmarks, dose-response curve\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"四点 differentiation 清晰且无重叠。我们使用 Wang et al. 的 model zoo（proper attribution）但提供了他们完全没有的分析维度。这回应 Reviewer Risk 4 和 Concern E， 将我们的贡献从\\\"also studied convergence\\\"提升到\\\"discovered and characterized a phenomenon they only glimpsed qualitatively\\\"。\\n\\n\\nWang et al. 的论文是 model zoo paper，核心贡献是训练并开源 72 个模型。他们对 convergence 的提及限于 qualitative observations（如 \\\"performance gap narrows with more attention layers\\\"），没有 (a) 计算 cross-arch std trajectories 或 Spearman ρ，(b) 做 per-example analysis，(c) 分析 scale dependency of convergence， (d) 提供 mechanistic explanation。我们的增量恰好是他们没做的四件事。这四点 differentiation 在 paper 中以 explicit side-by-side table 呈现，让 reviewer 一目了然。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"在 LAMBADA 上，以 attention ratio 为 x 轴，同时绘制 aggregate convergence（cross-arch std） 和 per-example divergence（Jaccard, net effect asymmetry），展示 paradox 的共同演化。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"convergence_divergence_correlation\": -0.94,\n      \"convergence_divergence_p\": 0.005,\n      \"paradox_strengthens_with_attention\": true,\n      \"jaccard_at_ratio_0\": \"N/A (no attention effect)\",\n      \"jaccard_at_ratio_1\": 0.08,\n      \"jaccard_at_ratio_6\": 0.06,\n      \"jaccard_at_ratio_24\": 0.04,\n      \"std_at_ratio_0\": 0.024,\n      \"std_at_ratio_24\": 0.005,\n      \"net_effect_asymmetry_gdn\": -0.12,\n      \"net_effect_asymmetry_retnet\": -0.08,\n      \"net_effect_asymmetry_hgrn2\": 0.11\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 9: Convergence-divergence co-evolution by attention ratio\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Attention ratio\",\n          \"Cross-arch std\",\n          \"Jaccard (mean pairwise)\",\n          \"GDN net effect\",\n          \"RetNet net effect\",\n          \"HGRN2 net effect\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0 (pure recurrent)\",\n            \"0.024\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"0.00\",\n            \"0.00\",\n            \"0.00\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"1\",\n            \"0.018\",\n            \"0.08\",\n            \"-0.03\",\n            \"-0.02\",\n            \"+0.03\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"3\",\n            \"0.012\",\n            \"0.07\",\n            \"-0.06\",\n            \"-0.04\",\n            \"+0.06\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"6\",\n            \"0.008\",\n            \"0.06\",\n            \"-0.09\",\n            \"-0.06\",\n            \"+0.08\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"8\",\n            \"0.007\",\n            \"0.05\",\n            \"-0.10\",\n            \"-0.07\",\n            \"+0.10\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"24\",\n            \"0.005\",\n            \"0.04\",\n            \"-0.12\",\n            \"-0.08\",\n            \"+0.11\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Convergence-divergence co-evolution（r=-0.94, p=0.005）是 paper 的 hero result， 直接可视化了 title 中的 \\\"Equalizer Paradox\\\"。这不是一个偶然发现，而是 attention 作为\\\"equalizer\\\"的内在机制：它通过在不同架构上做不同的事来实现 aggregate 趋同。 Net effect asymmetry 的对称性（GDN/RetNet hurt, HGRN2 helped, 幅度近似）表明 convergence 不是某个架构\\\"被拉上来\\\"，而是所有架构\\\"被推向中间\\\"——这与 paper title \\\"Equalizer\\\" 的隐喻完美对应。此图应作为 paper 的 Figure 1 或 graphical abstract。\\n\\n随着 attention ratio 增加，aggregate convergence 增强（std 从 0.024 降到 0.005） 而 per-example divergence 也增强（Jaccard 从 0.08 降到 0.04，意味着 helped/hurt subsets 越来越不重叠）。两者负相关（r=-0.94）是 paradox 的数学必然：当各架构 的 aggregate 趋同但 per-example effect magnitude 增大时，唯一的解释是各架构在 不同 sample 上做了更大幅度的\\\"互补性\\\"调整。更多 attention = 更强的补偿效应 = aggregate 更趋同 + per-example 更 divergent。Net effect asymmetry（GDN 和 RetNet net negative, HGRN2 net positive）在所有 attention ratio 保持方向一致但幅度 随 ratio 增大，呈现对称但相反的效应——这就是 \\\"equalizer paradox\\\" 的核心可视化。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":644,"startLine":1,"totalLines":644}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GUYQD62hmCyQHeKqdnrhHf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019L2XKT3FWbZDjP2nfAPLij","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/entrainment_gated_ft/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260519T131014/best/paper_framing.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11718,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11718},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e458f2f1-96ec-4b1e-abae-2d80d2354b5b","uuid":"8f7e9be2-7af2-4e78-bdc1-d19f048cd11c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019L2XKT3FWbZDjP2nfAPLij","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — entrainment_gated_ft\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n5\t- Backup: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n6\t- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n7\t\n8\t## Paper Type\n9\tEmpirical analysis paper (not method paper)\n10\t\n11\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n12\t\n13\t### Claim 1: Task-Specific Equalizer Effect\n14\tAdding attention layers to different linear recurrent architectures (GatedDeltaNet, RetNet, HGRN2) induces aggregate performance convergence whose strength scales with task retrieval demand—strongest on LAMBADA (ρ=-1.0, cross-arch std drops 79%), suggestive on ARC-Easy (ρ=-0.7, underpowered), absent on reasoning-heavy tasks (HellaSwag, WinoGrande). This continuous relationship between retrieval demand and convergence strength is a key finding, not a limitation of single-task significance.\n15\t\n16\t### Claim 2: Scale-Dependent Convergence\n17\tThe convergence effect is scale-dependent: monotonically complete at 1.3B parameters (Spearman ρ=-1.0 for cross-arch std vs attention ratio, exact permutation p=0.0083) but only partial at 340M with a non-monotonic rebound at high attention ratios. Note: only two scale points available (Wang et al. do not provide 7B models); this is a binary contrast, not a multi-point trend. Paper must frame honestly as \"scale matters\" without implying extrapolation.\n18\t\n19\t### Claim 3: Architecture-Specific Mechanism (Equalizer Paradox)\n20\tDespite aggregate convergence, attention acts on almost entirely different sample subsets per architecture (pairwise Jaccard < 0.10). GDN and RetNet are hurt (net negative on LAMBADA), HGRN2 is helped (net positive), with symmetric effect magnitudes—convergence emerges from complementary, not redundant, mechanisms.\n21\t\n22\t## Story Spine\n23\t\n24\t### Problem\n25\tHybrid architectures mixing linear recurrence with full attention are becoming the dominant paradigm for efficient language models. A critical open question: does adding attention homogenize model behavior across different recurrence mechanisms, or do architecture-specific effects persist?\n26\t\n27\t### Existing Approaches & Gaps\n28\tWang et al. (2025, arXiv 2507.06457) provide the most comprehensive model zoo (72 models, 3 architectures, multiple scales and attention ratios) but report only aggregate metrics. They qualitatively note convergence trends but do not analyze: (a) the per-example mechanism, (b) scale dependency of convergence, (c) task-specificity, or (d) why architectures converge to similar *aggregate* performance through *different* individual-sample effects.\n29\t\n30\t### Our Framing\n31\tWe provide the first quantitative characterization of the \"equalizer effect\"—a systematic per-example analysis revealing that attention creates aggregate performance convergence through architecture-specific, largely non-overlapping mechanisms. This \"equalizer paradox\" (aggregate convergence + per-example divergence) has direct implications for architecture selection: even when aggregate metrics converge, the types of inputs each architecture handles well remain architecture-specific.\n32\t\n33\t### Headline Result Template\n34\t\"At 1.3B scale, adding attention layers reduces cross-architecture performance variance by 79% on LAMBADA (std 0.024→0.005), yet per-example analysis reveals the affected sample subsets are almost entirely non-overlapping across architectures (Jaccard < 0.10), with symmetric but opposite effect directions.\"\n35\t\n36\t## Venue Fit Risks\n37\t\n38\t### Risk 1: Architecture Analysis vs NLP\n39\tEMNLP is NLP-focused; this paper is closer to architecture analysis. **Mitigation**: Frame in terms of understanding language model behavior on specific linguistic tasks. Anchor analysis to token-level and context-level linguistic features (frequency, context length, retrieval demand). Include practical recommendations for practitioners choosing hybrid architectures for specific NLP tasks.\n40\t\n41\t### Risk 2: Limited Task Coverage\n42\tCurrently only LAMBADA shows clear convergence. **Mitigation**: (a) Extend per-example analysis to HellaSwag and other benchmarks, (b) provide principled explanation of LAMBADA's retrieval-dependent nature vs reasoning tasks, (c) if convergence appears on other retrieval tasks, strengthens Claim 1; if not, reframe as \"convergence is task-type-specific\" which is still interesting.\n43\t\n44\t### Risk 3: Small Architecture Sample\n45\tOnly 3 architectures (GDN, RetNet, HGRN2). **Mitigation**: These represent three distinct recurrence mechanisms (gated delta rule, linear attention with exponential decay, hierarchical gated recurrence). Check if Wang et al. have additional architectures or scales. n=3 is sufficient for the per-example analysis which is our main contribution.\n46\t\n47\t### Risk 4: Wang et al. Overlap\n48\tThey have the model zoo AND qualitative convergence observation. **Mitigation**: Our contribution is explicitly about what they did NOT do: quantitative convergence framework, scale-dependent analysis, per-example mechanism analysis. Frame as \"using their excellent model zoo, we discover a deeper phenomenon they missed.\"\n49\t\n50\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n51\t\n52\t### Concern A: \"This is just a negative result from a failed hypothesis\"\n53\tResponse: Frame as discovery paper. The equalizer effect is a positive finding—it was not the hypothesis we started with, but it's a genuine empirical phenomenon with theoretical implications. Many impactful papers come from unexpected findings.\n54\tRequired evidence: Strong standalone story; no mention of original entrainment hypothesis in the paper.\n55\t\n56\t### Concern B: \"Only one task shows the effect\" + Post-hoc taxonomy risk\n57\tResponse: Do NOT use binary retrieval/reasoning split — vulnerable to post-hoc cherry-picking (only 1 benchmark in \"retrieval\" category, exactly the one that's significant). Instead:\n58\t1. **Continuous spectrum**: Plot convergence strength (Spearman ρ) against a continuous measure of \"retrieval demand\" per benchmark. LAMBADA ρ=-1.0, ARC-E ρ=-0.7 (suggestive), ARC-C ρ=-0.3, HellaSwag/WinoGrande/MMLU near zero. Frame as dose-response: more retrieval demand → stronger convergence.\n59\t2. **Cite existing task taxonomies**: Use BIG-bench taxonomy or other published meta-analyses for task property classification — don't invent our own post-hoc.\n60\t3. **Honest reporting**: ARC-E ρ=-0.7 (p=0.117) is \"suggestive but underpowered\" — n=5 ratios means low statistical power. Continuous spectrum framing turns \"only LAMBADA significant\" into \"graded effect consistent with retrieval demand.\"\n61\t4. **Winogrande ambiguity**: Coreference resolution has a retrieval component (finding antecedent). Acknowledge this honestly rather than forcing it into \"reasoning.\"\n62\t5. **exp-002 validation**: If HellaSwag per-example analysis confirms no convergence at sample level, upgrades from \"aggregate not significant\" to \"per-example confirmed non-converging.\"\n63\tRequired experiments: exp-001 (done, PASS on dichotomy), exp-002 (per-example validation), exp-003 (sample characterization).\n64\t\n65\t### Concern C: \"No causal mechanism\"\n66\tResponse: Per-example analysis provides mechanistic evidence (different subsets). Strengthen with attention weight visualization and sample feature characterization.\n67\tRequired experiments: Sample characterization (exp-003), attention weight analysis (exp-004).\n68\t\n69\t### Concern D: \"n=3 architectures is too few\"\n70\tResponse: Three architectures with 5 attention ratios × 2 scales = 30 models. The per-example analysis provides thousands of data points. Check if additional architectures available.\n71\tRequired experiments: Architecture expansion check (exp-005).\n72\t\n73\t### Concern E: \"Two scales don't establish a trend\"\n74\tResponse: 7B unavailable (Wang et al. capped at 1.3B). Frame as \"binary contrast showing scale is a necessary condition\" — convergence requires sufficient model capacity (1.3B), not just attention. Strengthen via exp-007 (340M rebound mechanism analysis) to provide mechanistic explanation for the scale gap. Acknowledge as limitation; do not imply extrapolation.\n75\tRequired experiments: exp-007 (340M rebound mechanism).\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e458f2f1-96ec-4b1e-abae-2d80d2354b5b","uuid":"8794b6e2-2f96-4e36-929e-3cc3170615da","timestamp":"2026-05-19T13:28:20.978Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/entrainment_gated_ft/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260519T131014/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — entrainment_gated_ft\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n- Backup: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n\n## Paper Type\nEmpirical analysis paper (not method paper)\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n### Claim 1: Task-Specific Equalizer Effect\nAdding attention layers to different linear recurrent architectures (GatedDeltaNet, RetNet, HGRN2) induces aggregate performance convergence whose strength scales with task retrieval demand—strongest on LAMBADA (ρ=-1.0, cross-arch std drops 79%), suggestive on ARC-Easy (ρ=-0.7, underpowered), absent on reasoning-heavy tasks (HellaSwag, WinoGrande). This continuous relationship between retrieval demand and convergence strength is a key finding, not a limitation of single-task significance.\n\n### Claim 2: Scale-Dependent Convergence\nThe convergence effect is scale-dependent: monotonically complete at 1.3B parameters (Spearman ρ=-1.0 for cross-arch std vs attention ratio, exact permutation p=0.0083) but only partial at 340M with a non-monotonic rebound at high attention ratios. Note: only two scale points available (Wang et al. do not provide 7B models); this is a binary contrast, not a multi-point trend. Paper must frame honestly as \"scale matters\" without implying extrapolation.\n\n### Claim 3: Architecture-Specific Mechanism (Equalizer Paradox)\nDespite aggregate convergence, attention acts on almost entirely different sample subsets per architecture (pairwise Jaccard < 0.10). GDN and RetNet are hurt (net negative on LAMBADA), HGRN2 is helped (net positive), with symmetric effect magnitudes—convergence emerges from complementary, not redundant, mechanisms.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n### Problem\nHybrid architectures mixing linear recurrence with full attention are becoming the dominant paradigm for efficient language models. A critical open question: does adding attention homogenize model behavior across different recurrence mechanisms, or do architecture-specific effects persist?\n\n### Existing Approaches & Gaps\nWang et al. (2025, arXiv 2507.06457) provide the most comprehensive model zoo (72 models, 3 architectures, multiple scales and attention ratios) but report only aggregate metrics. They qualitatively note convergence trends but do not analyze: (a) the per-example mechanism, (b) scale dependency of convergence, (c) task-specificity, or (d) why architectures converge to similar *aggregate* performance through *different* individual-sample effects.\n\n### Our Framing\nWe provide the first quantitative characterization of the \"equalizer effect\"—a systematic per-example analysis revealing that attention creates aggregate performance convergence through architecture-specific, largely non-overlapping mechanisms. This \"equalizer paradox\" (aggregate convergence + per-example divergence) has direct implications for architecture selection: even when aggregate metrics converge, the types of inputs each architecture handles well remain architecture-specific.\n\n### Headline Result Template\n\"At 1.3B scale, adding attention layers reduces cross-architecture performance variance by 79% on LAMBADA (std 0.024→0.005), yet per-example analysis reveals the affected sample subsets are almost entirely non-overlapping across architectures (Jaccard < 0.10), with symmetric but opposite effect directions.\"\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n### Risk 1: Architecture Analysis vs NLP\nEMNLP is NLP-focused; this paper is closer to architecture analysis. **Mitigation**: Frame in terms of understanding language model behavior on specific linguistic tasks. Anchor analysis to token-level and context-level linguistic features (frequency, context length, retrieval demand). Include practical recommendations for practitioners choosing hybrid architectures for specific NLP tasks.\n\n### Risk 2: Limited Task Coverage\nCurrently only LAMBADA shows clear convergence. **Mitigation**: (a) Extend per-example analysis to HellaSwag and other benchmarks, (b) provide principled explanation of LAMBADA's retrieval-dependent nature vs reasoning tasks, (c) if convergence appears on other retrieval tasks, strengthens Claim 1; if not, reframe as \"convergence is task-type-specific\" which is still interesting.\n\n### Risk 3: Small Architecture Sample\nOnly 3 architectures (GDN, RetNet, HGRN2). **Mitigation**: These represent three distinct recurrence mechanisms (gated delta rule, linear attention with exponential decay, hierarchical gated recurrence). Check if Wang et al. have additional architectures or scales. n=3 is sufficient for the per-example analysis which is our main contribution.\n\n### Risk 4: Wang et al. Overlap\nThey have the model zoo AND qualitative convergence observation. **Mitigation**: Our contribution is explicitly about what they did NOT do: quantitative convergence framework, scale-dependent analysis, per-example mechanism analysis. Frame as \"using their excellent model zoo, we discover a deeper phenomenon they missed.\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### Concern A: \"This is just a negative result from a failed hypothesis\"\nResponse: Frame as discovery paper. The equalizer effect is a positive finding—it was not the hypothesis we started with, but it's a genuine empirical phenomenon with theoretical implications. Many impactful papers come from unexpected findings.\nRequired evidence: Strong standalone story; no mention of original entrainment hypothesis in the paper.\n\n### Concern B: \"Only one task shows the effect\" + Post-hoc taxonomy risk\nResponse: Do NOT use binary retrieval/reasoning split — vulnerable to post-hoc cherry-picking (only 1 benchmark in \"retrieval\" category, exactly the one that's significant). Instead:\n1. **Continuous spectrum**: Plot convergence strength (Spearman ρ) against a continuous measure of \"retrieval demand\" per benchmark. LAMBADA ρ=-1.0, ARC-E ρ=-0.7 (suggestive), ARC-C ρ=-0.3, HellaSwag/WinoGrande/MMLU near zero. Frame as dose-response: more retrieval demand → stronger convergence.\n2. **Cite existing task taxonomies**: Use BIG-bench taxonomy or other published meta-analyses for task property classification — don't invent our own post-hoc.\n3. **Honest reporting**: ARC-E ρ=-0.7 (p=0.117) is \"suggestive but underpowered\" — n=5 ratios means low statistical power. Continuous spectrum framing turns \"only LAMBADA significant\" into \"graded effect consistent with retrieval demand.\"\n4. **Winogrande ambiguity**: Coreference resolution has a retrieval component (finding antecedent). Acknowledge this honestly rather than forcing it into \"reasoning.\"\n5. **exp-002 validation**: If HellaSwag per-example analysis confirms no convergence at sample level, upgrades from \"aggregate not significant\" to \"per-example confirmed non-converging.\"\nRequired experiments: exp-001 (done, PASS on dichotomy), exp-002 (per-example validation), exp-003 (sample characterization).\n\n### Concern C: \"No causal mechanism\"\nResponse: Per-example analysis provides mechanistic evidence (different subsets). Strengthen with attention weight visualization and sample feature characterization.\nRequired experiments: Sample characterization (exp-003), attention weight analysis (exp-004).\n\n### Concern D: \"n=3 architectures is too few\"\nResponse: Three architectures with 5 attention ratios × 2 scales = 30 models. The per-example analysis provides thousands of data points. Check if additional architectures available.\nRequired experiments: Architecture expansion check (exp-005).\n\n### Concern E: \"Two scales don't establish a trend\"\nResponse: 7B unavailable (Wang et al. capped at 1.3B). Frame as \"binary contrast showing scale is a necessary condition\" — convergence requires sufficient model capacity (1.3B), not just attention. Strengthen via exp-007 (340M rebound mechanism analysis) to provide mechanistic explanation for the scale gap. Acknowledge as limitation; do not imply extrapolation.\nRequired experiments: exp-007 (340M rebound mechanism).\n","numLines":76,"startLine":1,"totalLines":76}}}
